---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<ContentLayout
  title="About This Starter"
  description="An architectural overview and guiding principles behind this production-ready Astro + TypeScript template."
  author={siteConfig.author.name}
  backLink={{ href: '/', label: 'Back to Homepage' }}
>
  <p>
    The <strong>Astro + TypeScript Starter</strong> was engineered to bridge the gap between simple
    single-purpose templates and bloated multi-framework setups. It provides an unopinionated,
    high-performance foundation that can easily be adapted for company profile sites, developer
    portfolios, blogs, documentation portals, or SaaS landing pages.
  </p>

  <h2>Core Architectural Tenets</h2>

  <h3>1. Static-First Performance</h3>
  <p>
    By default, pages render at build time into pure HTML and CSS. There are no heavy client-side
    JavaScript runtimes, no virtual DOM diffing, and no unnecessary client hydration. This
    guarantees near-instant page loads and top-tier Core Web Vitals (LCP, INP, CLS).
  </p>

  <h3>2. Complete Type Safety</h3>
  <p>
    The template enables strict TypeScript checks across the entire codebase. From component props
    and site configurations to content collection schemas, every data contract is typed and
    validated.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Zero-FOUC Theming & Design Tokens</h3>
  <p>
    Rather than relying on runtime CSS-in-JS libraries or external utility frameworks, all design
    tokens are exposed as standard CSS custom properties in <code>tokens.css</code>. Light and dark
    themes are supported seamlessly with an instant inline script in the document{' '}
    <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>, guaranteeing zero flash of unstyled content (FOUC).
  </p>

  <h3>4. Accessible and SEO-Optimized</h3>
  <p>Accessibility and SEO are treated as first-class citizens. Key features include:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Automated Open Graph and Twitter Card metadata generation.</li>
    <li>Canonical URL normalization.</li>
    <li>
      Dynamic sitemap generation via <code>@astrojs/sitemap</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      A dedicated <code>robots.txt.ts</code> endpoint.
    </li>
    <li>Accessible skip links, semantic landmarks, and WCAG AA contrast compliance.</li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <h2>Open Source & Extensible</h2>
  <p>
    This project is released under the permissive <strong>MIT License</strong>. Feel free to use it
    as the boilerplate for your personal or commercial projects.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
